    {
      "end": "finished",
      "end_summary": "Fixed the bug in Union trait default value handling. The issue had two root causes:\n\n1. In `traits/ctraits.c`: The `CONSTANT_DEFAULT_VALUE` was incorrectly defined as 0 instead of 7, causing the DefaultValue.constant enum to have the wrong value (0 instead of 7).\n\n2. In `traits/trait_types.py`: In the Union.__init__ method, the variables were swapped when unpacking the result from `default_value()` - it was assigning `first_default_value, first_default_value_type = ...` when the method returns `(default_value_type, default_value)`.\n\nFixed both issues:\n- Changed `#define CONSTANT_DEFAULT_VALUE 0` to `#define CONSTANT_DEFAULT_VALUE 7` in `traits/ctraits.c` \n- Swapped the variable names to `first_default_value_type, first_default_value = ...` in `traits/trait_types.py`\n- Had to also adjust `CALLABLE_AND_ARGS_DEFAULT_VALUE` from 7 to 15 to avoid duplicate case values in the C switch statement\n\nThe fix ensures that when Union inherits from a class and gets overridden with a literal value (like `foo = 5`), the trait initialization works correctly and the trait behaves as expected.",
